  = must: preserve this decision as a deferral, not a rejection of future manager adapters, coordination adapters, operations adapters, transports, UI, dispatch mechanisms, telemetry, schedulers, LangGraph runtime integration, Langflow projection, or future Ryzen 9 RTX 5090 operations-manager capability
  = must: require a later explicit activation slice before adding package dependencies, lockfiles, imports from external adapter packages, socket listeners, chat clients, Matrix clients, IRC clients, web servers, LangGraph runtime adapters, Langflow exports, MCP clients, MCP servers, job queues, scheduler clients, telemetry collectors, process controllers, GPU controllers, model runtime clients, credential readers, network mutators, or persistent manager automation
  = must: require a separate future source-preserved and SJS-processed dispatch authority path before any manager, agent, or job dispatch can be reconsidered
  = must: require a separate future source-preserved and SJS-processed live-control authority path before any live machine control can be reconsidered
  = must: keep SOP, SJS, completion reviews, accepted decision documents, tracked fixture sources, expected ledgers, and canonical specifications as source authority
  = must: treat manager packets, readiness projections, handoff records, refusal records, fault records, operation requests, dry-run results, carrier messages, terminal output, chat events, telemetry, graph checkpoints, generated reports, adapter callbacks, UI state, and dispatch attempts as projections or evidence until rewritten into accepted SOP authority by a later reviewed process

