& [AuthorityBoundaryAssessment: IR8ManagerAdapters] is the authority fit assessment for future manager surfaces
  + [fit_status] is future_adapter_candidates_preserved
  + [fit_reason] is manager adapters, coordination adapters, operations adapters, chat transports, UI surfaces, LangGraph runtime execution, Langflow projection, schedulers, telemetry, and future machine-management integrations may become useful projections or controlled execution surfaces after authority-preserving boundaries exist
  + [mismatch_status] is authority_boundary_mismatch_if_used_directly_as_truth
  + [mismatch_reason] is manager packet readiness, operation dry-run state, coordination carrier state, resource telemetry, process state, GPU state, model runtime state, job queues, terminal output, chat commands, adapter callbacks, UI events, graph checkpoints, generated reports, and dispatch attempts are projections or execution state rather than accepted SOP authority
  + [adapter_need] is map accepted LangSOP authority records into adapter inputs and map adapter outputs back into non-authoritative manager observations, operation requests, human override records, resource safety reviews, refusal records, SOP-first interrupts, dependency decisions, or completion reviews until accepted by SOP review

  = must: prevent packet readiness, dry-run success, carrier delivery success, telemetry availability, generated report success, approval display state, adapter callback success, UI click, chat command, terminal output, or graph execution success from satisfying readiness, completion review, source specification processing, dispatch authority, operations authority, or live-control gates by itself
  = must: preserve human override, human approval, conflict review, resource safety review, and completion review as reviewed SOP records rather than direct UI, transport, mailbox, terminal, adapter, or dispatch effects

